WEBVTT

00:00.950 --> 00:04.580
Hey, what color do you 
think Hori-senpai would like?

00:05.480 --> 00:09.230
<b>Chocolate Recipes</b>

00:05.480 --> 00:09.230
I've seen her with red 
and pink things before...

00:09.730 --> 00:12.240
Maybe that would be 
better than blue or white.

00:13.590 --> 00:15.490
Hey, are you listening?

00:15.490 --> 00:17.430
Are you listening, Miyamura?!

00:17.430 --> 00:18.490
Please leave.

00:18.840 --> 00:20.590
Miyamura, you're her boyfriend!

00:20.590 --> 00:21.790
Please leave.

00:21.790 --> 00:24.870
So what color does she like?

00:24.870 --> 00:26.750
Sawada-san, please leave.

00:26.750 --> 00:28.860
Valentine's Day is almost here,

00:26.750 --> 00:34.010
<b><i>SNAP</i></b>

00:28.860 --> 00:31.990
and I can't wrap her present unless 
I know what color ribbon to use!

00:31.990 --> 00:34.010
Why did you come to ask me?!

00:34.430 --> 00:36.620
Maybe you just don't understand 
how important it is

00:36.620 --> 00:39.580
for a present to be as cute 
and appealing as possible.

00:39.580 --> 00:42.770
I mean, maybe I don't, but...

00:43.310 --> 00:44.890
The wrapping, huh?

00:45.990 --> 00:47.400
Miyamura, don't tell me...

00:48.060 --> 00:50.800
Are you planning to just 
let the shop wrap it?

00:52.060 --> 00:54.870
Well, not that it's any of my business.

00:55.550 --> 00:57.410
But the shop's wrapping is cute...

00:57.940 --> 00:59.740
How do you do it, Sawada?

00:59.740 --> 01:02.910
Hmm, what color should I pick?

01:03.720 --> 01:07.010
Hori-san likes red and orange.

01:08.190 --> 01:10.170
That'll do.

01:10.290 --> 01:13.960
<b>Chocolate</b>

01:10.850 --> 01:13.960
This wrapping is simple and 
looks cute, don't you think?

02:44.010 --> 02:47.020
<b>Katagiri High School</b>

02:48.940 --> 02:50.690
Good morning, Sawada-san.

02:50.690 --> 02:51.680
Good morning.

02:51.680 --> 02:53.020
G-Good morning.

02:55.890 --> 02:59.940
<i>Oh, right. I need to figure out 
where to buy a ribbon.</i>

03:07.020 --> 03:10.920
Kyon-Kyon, you're gonna give 
Miyamura-kun a Valentine, right?

03:10.920 --> 03:14.490
Nope, he said he's making one for me.

03:14.820 --> 03:17.660
Miyamura-kun's family
owns a cake shop, right?

03:17.660 --> 03:19.420
I bet he'll make something really nice.

03:20.610 --> 03:22.040
What about you, Kyon-Kyon?

03:22.040 --> 03:23.340
Me?

03:23.340 --> 03:26.180
I don't think I can make a very good dessert.

03:26.180 --> 03:29.090
Oh. That's kinda selfish.

03:26.430 --> 03:29.930
<b>Stare</b>

03:30.530 --> 03:33.940
I mean, mine would pale 
in comparison to Miyamura's,

03:33.940 --> 03:36.820
<b>Famous Pâtissier</b>

03:34.330 --> 03:36.820
and it won't feel right to give him 
one from a different shop.

03:34.690 --> 03:36.820
<b>Big-Chain Bakery</b>

03:36.820 --> 03:39.660
That's the wrong way to think about it.

03:36.860 --> 03:45.320
<b>The last cake she made was burned to a crisp

<i>Smolder Smolder</i></b>

03:39.660 --> 03:42.380
He'll be so disappointed.

03:42.380 --> 03:45.320
He doesn't want to be gifted
 a crappy dessert!

03:45.780 --> 03:49.710
I think he'd be happy
to receive anything you made.

03:52.580 --> 03:55.590
<i>I still think a good dessert would be better.</i>

03:54.170 --> 03:55.590
The one on this page, okay?

03:55.590 --> 03:56.590
Okay.

03:55.960 --> 03:57.980
Oh, Sawada-san?

03:57.710 --> 03:59.590
<b>WHIP</b>

03:58.310 --> 03:59.590
Hori-senpai!

04:00.060 --> 04:01.260
You over here for class?

04:00.970 --> 04:01.740
<i><b>Zoom</b></i>

04:01.260 --> 04:03.430
No, I just needed to show Miyamura something.

04:03.790 --> 04:06.360
But, say, it's almost time, isn't it?

04:06.360 --> 04:08.310
I'll do my best this year!

04:08.310 --> 04:09.100
Huh?

04:09.100 --> 04:11.850
I got Miyamura to tell me—

04:11.390 --> 04:11.480
<b>WH</b>

04:11.390 --> 04:11.480
<b>AP</b>

04:11.580 --> 04:11.850
<b>WH</b>

04:11.580 --> 04:11.850
<b>AP</b>

04:11.850 --> 04:14.620
Wriggle Struggle

04:11.850 --> 04:15.100
Come on, Sawada-san.
You don't want to be late for class.

04:15.100 --> 04:16.870
What're you doing?!

04:15.100 --> 04:19.020
<i>I can't have her finding out 
I can't decide on the gift wrap!</i>

04:16.870 --> 04:19.020
Hori-senpai!

04:19.330 --> 04:21.190
What was that about?

04:21.190 --> 04:22.520
No idea.

04:23.790 --> 04:24.610
<i>Gosh!</i>

04:24.610 --> 04:27.380
<i>He could be a little more understanding!</i>

04:27.710 --> 04:30.440
<i>I'm getting mad just thinking about it!</i>

04:30.440 --> 04:32.370
Um, Sawada-san?

04:34.460 --> 04:35.370
Yes?

04:37.500 --> 04:41.130
Um, you're friends with 
the third-years, right?

04:42.470 --> 04:43.820
<i>This again?</i>

04:43.820 --> 04:45.150
Yeah, I am.

04:45.800 --> 04:47.140
What about it?

04:47.450 --> 04:49.890
Valentine's Day is coming up.

04:49.890 --> 04:50.790
Yeah.

04:50.790 --> 04:52.140
So I was, um...

04:52.140 --> 04:54.650
There's a third-year boy...

04:56.400 --> 04:58.150
<b>Yanagi</b>

04:56.400 --> 04:58.150
Well... he's pretty cool

04:56.400 --> 04:58.150
<b>Miyamura</b>

04:56.400 --> 04:58.150
Well... he's not bad

04:58.150 --> 04:59.460
Which one?

04:59.460 --> 05:01.390
Huh? Wh-Which one?

05:01.390 --> 05:03.400
You mean Yanagi or Miyamura, right?

05:03.400 --> 05:05.150
I can pass a present to either one.

05:05.150 --> 05:08.660
Wh-Who are Yanagi and Miyamura?

05:11.540 --> 05:13.160
An underclassman
says she likes him,
 I think...

05:11.540 --> 05:13.160
<b>Ishikawa</b>

05:12.040 --> 05:13.160
Well... he stands out

05:12.040 --> 05:13.160
<b>Sengoku</b>

05:13.160 --> 05:14.900
Ishikawa?

05:15.290 --> 05:16.380
Sengoku?

05:16.380 --> 05:19.170
S-Sorry, I don't know them either.

05:19.570 --> 05:23.520
Sorry, then it might be a boy I don't know.

05:23.940 --> 05:25.820
Oh, I see.

05:25.820 --> 05:28.930
He comes to school in a hoodie all the time.

05:29.430 --> 05:32.430
Oh, you mean Iura...

05:32.680 --> 05:33.140
<b>SHOCK</b>

05:32.800 --> 05:34.180
Wait, Iura?!

05:34.590 --> 05:39.250
Oh, I'm sorry. Do you also happen to...

05:39.250 --> 05:41.460
No, it's not like that.

05:41.460 --> 05:44.820
I-It's just... Iura?
The loudmouth in the hoodie?

05:44.820 --> 05:45.690
Yeah.

05:45.690 --> 05:54.450
<b>Rude</b>

05:47.840 --> 05:49.050
Seriously?

05:49.050 --> 05:49.910
Yeah.

05:49.910 --> 05:52.100
So his name is Iura-senpai?

05:52.100 --> 05:54.450
Gosh, I'm blushing...

05:54.450 --> 05:58.100
I've never spoken to him, and he 
probably doesn't know who I am,

05:54.450 --> 06:02.710
<b>GUSH GUSH GUSH</b>

05:58.100 --> 06:00.990
but I thought giving him 
some chocolate wouldn't hurt.

06:00.990 --> 06:02.960
He won't be here next year anyway.

06:02.960 --> 06:06.100
O-Okay, it's all good. Just calm down.

06:06.450 --> 06:09.470
Will he still accept it 
if he has a girlfriend?

06:09.470 --> 06:10.950
He doesn't have a girlfriend.

06:10.950 --> 06:12.190
R-Really?

06:12.190 --> 06:13.690
Not even secretly?

06:13.690 --> 06:14.720
Trust me.

06:14.720 --> 06:17.160
Do you want to date him? Why not tell him?

06:17.160 --> 06:19.720
D-Don't get the wrong idea.

06:19.720 --> 06:23.480
I j-just want to give him 
some chocolate. Th-That's all.

06:26.880 --> 06:28.240
I'm glad.

06:28.810 --> 06:31.470
I couldn't ask anyone in class.

06:31.970 --> 06:34.490
I really wanted to tell someone.

06:37.110 --> 06:39.250
Talking about it gets me sort of flustered.

06:40.970 --> 06:45.450
I-I'll listen, even if I can't do much.

06:45.450 --> 06:49.260
U-Um, I'd like you to ask what 
kind of chocolate he likes.

06:50.860 --> 06:53.600
You really only want to 
give him some chocolate?

06:53.600 --> 06:54.260
Yeah.

06:55.760 --> 06:57.690
So you respect him.

06:57.690 --> 06:59.680
That's it. That sounds right.

07:00.270 --> 07:01.770
<b>Student Council</b>

07:00.680 --> 07:05.270
The supermarkets and convenience stores are 
gonna start pushing Valentine's Day stuff.

07:05.270 --> 07:06.950
I feel you.

07:07.460 --> 07:11.670
But since you're probably gonna get a ton
of chocolate and I'm not, I <i>don't</i> feel you!

07:11.670 --> 07:14.030
You just said you did.

07:14.030 --> 07:16.760
Anyway, what are you two doing?

07:16.760 --> 07:17.610
Beats me.

07:17.610 --> 07:20.040
Practicing tying a tie, maybe?

07:20.040 --> 07:22.320
Miyamura can already tie a tie, right?

07:22.320 --> 07:24.560
I'm pretty sure he can.

07:24.560 --> 07:25.480
Done!

07:26.090 --> 07:28.050
Messy

07:28.300 --> 07:30.410
Wait... It's not cute at all.

07:30.410 --> 07:31.800
What's this supposed to be?

07:32.190 --> 07:35.300
<i>I thought I followed the directions 
from Sawada's magazine...</i>

07:35.300 --> 07:36.920
What even is this?

07:36.920 --> 07:40.520
Damn, the knot's too tight! 
I can't get it out, Miyamura!

07:41.060 --> 07:43.560
Hey, it's Sawada-san!

07:43.920 --> 07:45.040
What's up?

07:45.040 --> 07:46.110
Want me to get Miyamura?

07:46.110 --> 07:47.440
N-No.

07:47.440 --> 07:48.320
Sawada?

07:50.070 --> 07:51.740
I'm here to see...

07:52.100 --> 07:52.970
Iura.

07:52.970 --> 07:54.300
Huh? Me?

07:54.300 --> 07:55.150
Why?

07:55.150 --> 07:58.950
Um, do you like... chocolate?

08:00.950 --> 08:03.710
<b><i>S
H
O
C
K</i></b>

08:03.710 --> 08:06.960
<i>C-Could this be...</i>

08:07.490 --> 08:09.210
<i>in preparation for Valentine's Day?</i>

08:09.210 --> 08:10.710
S-Sure, I like chocolate.

08:10.710 --> 08:12.340
Any flavor in particular?

08:12.340 --> 08:13.680
I like them all.

08:13.680 --> 08:16.450
I don't have any allergies,
 and I can do sweet or bitter.

08:18.190 --> 08:20.720
<i>Everyone can see how desperate you are, Shu.</i>

08:21.040 --> 08:22.730
Any kind of chocolate is fine.

08:22.730 --> 08:24.350
Okay, thanks.

08:24.690 --> 08:25.100
Glance

08:25.440 --> 08:25.850
Glance

08:26.860 --> 08:28.610
Any kind at all!

08:29.030 --> 08:31.750
Sawada-san, are you 
gonna give Shu chocolate?

08:31.750 --> 08:33.530
I thought it'd just be Hori-san.

08:33.530 --> 08:36.770
H-H-Hey! Don't discourage her, you guys!

08:36.770 --> 08:39.520
Don't let them give you a hard time, okay?

08:40.120 --> 08:43.870
<i><b>Recoil</b></i>

08:40.690 --> 08:43.870
Why would <i>I</i> give chocolate to Iura?

08:43.960 --> 08:45.370
<b><i>S
H
O
C
K</i></b>

08:45.370 --> 08:47.350
That's crazy.

08:47.780 --> 08:49.380
Anyway, I'm heading back to class.

08:53.010 --> 08:55.640
Huh? Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-What was that?!

08:53.010 --> 09:00.140
<b>Confused</b>

08:54.620 --> 08:56.990
She's toying with your heart, Shu.

08:56.990 --> 08:58.640
I knew something didn't seem right.

09:02.640 --> 09:05.140
He said he likes any kind of chocolate.

09:05.480 --> 09:09.390
That's good. That means I can 
take my time picking some out.

09:09.390 --> 09:11.490
There are so many kinds, it's hard to choose.

09:11.490 --> 09:13.650
I didn't expect so many.

09:13.650 --> 09:16.300
Thanks for coming with me.

09:16.300 --> 09:17.250
It's nothing.

09:17.250 --> 09:20.910
I'm giving someone chocolate, too, 
so I wanted to see what they have.

09:20.910 --> 09:23.410
Who are you giving chocolate?

09:23.410 --> 09:25.120
I-It's a secret!

09:33.290 --> 09:36.430
If I'm not able to give it to him, 
will you accept it instead?

09:36.430 --> 09:38.460
Don't worry. You can do it!

09:38.460 --> 09:39.630
You're doing this for real!

09:41.030 --> 09:42.200
I'll do my best.

09:51.340 --> 09:53.230
<i>Valentine's Day is coming up.</i>

09:58.210 --> 10:01.990
I think he'd be happy
to receive anything you made.

10:04.210 --> 10:05.150
Okay.

10:06.000 --> 10:08.000
<b>Library</b>

10:07.300 --> 10:08.000
Wh...

10:08.000 --> 10:12.000
What's the easiest chocolate dessert to make?

10:14.000 --> 10:16.830
Oh, are you making 
a Valentine for Miyamura-kun?

10:16.830 --> 10:19.730
Shh! Someone might hear!

10:19.730 --> 10:22.260
It's okay. There's no one else here.

10:24.430 --> 10:27.520
I figured it would be best 
not to ask the person I'm giving it to.

10:28.440 --> 10:33.020
I know I won't be able to make
something nice like they sell in shops.

10:33.550 --> 10:37.530
But if there's a dessert I can't screw up...

10:37.530 --> 10:42.110
<i>Am I really gonna give the simplest dessert 
possible to a cake shop owner's son?</i>

10:38.070 --> 10:47.290
<b>Conflicted</b>

10:42.530 --> 10:45.400
As simple as possible, but still delicious...

10:47.290 --> 10:48.540
Hang on.

10:50.540 --> 10:52.540
<b>Simple Desserts to Make at Home</b>

10:52.540 --> 10:55.530
A recipe book? I didn't know 
the library had those.

10:55.530 --> 10:56.680
They do.

10:56.680 --> 10:59.300
And this one's easy to follow, too.

11:00.190 --> 11:03.800
When I started making desserts, 
I borrowed this book a lot.

11:04.970 --> 11:08.310
Chocolate desserts are... here, on this page.

11:08.310 --> 11:10.480
I think this one might work.

11:10.480 --> 11:13.020
<i>Kono-san's desserts are fantastic,</i>

11:12.560 --> 11:15.820
<b>Simple Desserts to Make at Home</b>

11:13.020 --> 11:14.960
<i>but I guess even she started somewhere.</i>

11:15.820 --> 11:16.570
<b><i>BAM</i></b>

11:16.610 --> 11:17.320
<b><i>BOOM</i></b>

11:17.360 --> 11:18.070
<b><i>BANG</i></b>

11:18.360 --> 11:19.280
<b><i>POW</i></b>

11:18.500 --> 11:19.670
Okay!

11:19.670 --> 11:21.950
Kyoko-chan, can I eat this?

11:21.950 --> 11:23.550
Get out!

11:23.550 --> 11:27.370
Honey, let Kyoko be when 
she's wielding a knife.

11:27.690 --> 11:29.960
Is she preparing for battle?

11:31.110 --> 11:33.960
Big Sis, what are you making?

11:33.960 --> 11:36.460
It's dangerous, so wait over there.

11:36.460 --> 11:38.420
Is it a special occasion?

11:38.420 --> 11:39.980
Not really.

11:39.980 --> 11:42.470
I'm just practicing for Valentine's Day.

11:42.910 --> 11:45.650
She says she's practicing for 
Valentine's Day with that scary face!

11:45.650 --> 11:47.130
Is she gonna fight someone?

11:47.130 --> 11:50.980
Dang it! I'll bring it to you when it's done,
 so let me concentrate!

11:52.620 --> 11:54.410
Scary!

11:55.670 --> 11:59.990
<i>I only look scary because 
I'm taking this so seriously.</i>

12:00.850 --> 12:05.620
<i>Miyamura will like it more 
if it tastes good.</i>

12:15.930 --> 12:17.000
It's not really good.

12:19.500 --> 12:22.010
I... I... I see...

12:22.010 --> 12:23.350
Sota, you dummy!

12:24.510 --> 12:26.660
I-I'll have one, too!

12:26.660 --> 12:28.510
No, don't!

12:28.510 --> 12:31.070
I'll try one.

12:31.070 --> 12:33.020
I think I will as well.

12:33.020 --> 12:35.270
No, don't!

12:38.270 --> 12:40.200
It's not so bad.

12:40.200 --> 12:42.460
I just can't eat a lot of it.

12:42.460 --> 12:44.030
It's not terrible?

12:45.210 --> 12:48.350
I can see why Sota wouldn't like it.

12:48.350 --> 12:50.540
It's not too sweet.

12:51.210 --> 12:52.890
It's perfect for me, though.

12:52.890 --> 12:54.040
I'll have another.

12:54.040 --> 12:57.040
Hey, Yuri-chan's going for the biggest one!

12:57.040 --> 12:59.040
I-It's good?

12:59.040 --> 13:00.380
It depends on your taste.

12:59.040 --> 13:03.300
<b><i>BA-BAM</i></b>

13:00.380 --> 13:02.720
Tell me if it's good or not!

13:05.300 --> 13:08.300
Glooooom

13:08.300 --> 13:11.050
A-Are you okay, Hori-san?

13:11.050 --> 13:13.660
I must be lacking taste.

13:13.660 --> 13:16.570
That kind of thinking won't get you anywhere.

13:20.240 --> 13:23.070
I don't think you need to worry.

13:24.730 --> 13:28.320
Guys don't mind things a little bitter.

13:28.710 --> 13:30.710
Tell it to me straight!

13:30.710 --> 13:33.180
I promise not to fly into a rage.

13:33.180 --> 13:35.330
You're already getting hysterical!

13:35.330 --> 13:39.090
I didn't even cut them right.

13:40.340 --> 13:43.010
Hori-san, remember what Remi said?

13:44.200 --> 13:48.090
He'll be happy to receive anything you made.

13:49.270 --> 13:55.340
It not how it looks or how 
it tastes that matters most.

13:55.850 --> 13:59.350
And personally, I like this chocolate.

13:59.900 --> 14:01.700
It reminds me of you.

14:04.110 --> 14:05.830
Kono-san...

14:05.830 --> 14:08.270
Hori-san, why are you behind me?

14:09.060 --> 14:13.430
<i>She's right. The most important thing is...</i>

14:14.440 --> 14:15.870
Happy Valentine's Day.

14:15.870 --> 14:17.780
I'm blushing.

14:17.780 --> 14:18.720
Thanks.

14:18.720 --> 14:20.770
J-Just so you know, 
I'm giving them to everyone!

14:20.770 --> 14:23.480
I know. It's fine.

14:24.260 --> 14:27.100
Iura-kun! Here's your obligatory chocolate.

14:27.100 --> 14:29.130
At least say it's friend-to-friend.

14:29.130 --> 14:31.350
Hey, it's Miyamura brand!

14:31.350 --> 14:32.890
Remember our shop's name, please.

14:33.570 --> 14:35.550
Hey, Miyamura, I want some, too!

14:33.570 --> 14:36.580
Looks like Miyamura-kun brought more 
chocolate than the girls.

14:35.550 --> 14:36.580
Coming!

14:36.930 --> 14:38.040
<i>You're telling me.</i>

14:38.640 --> 14:39.740
Hori-san.

14:40.390 --> 14:42.120
Can you come over today?

14:42.120 --> 14:43.390
Sure.

14:43.390 --> 14:45.160
Can I come after school?

14:45.160 --> 14:46.530
Yeah. Oh!

14:46.840 --> 14:50.780
But I'm heading home early,
 so take your time.

14:50.780 --> 14:53.620
Okay, then I'll stop by my place first.

14:53.620 --> 14:57.240
Let me know if it starts to 
get dark. I'll come get you.

14:57.240 --> 14:58.520
I'll be fine.

14:58.520 --> 15:00.290
Then I'll see you later.

15:01.150 --> 15:05.630
<i>It's gotta be chocolate. 
He said he'd make me some.</i>

15:05.630 --> 15:09.050
<i>But he almost always comes to our place...</i>

15:09.050 --> 15:12.050
<b>Giant Chocolate Fondue Tower</b>

15:09.050 --> 15:12.050
Wow!

15:10.390 --> 15:12.050
<i>Did he make something huge?</i>

15:12.460 --> 15:14.970
<i>What is it? I'm dying to know!</i>

15:14.970 --> 15:17.060
Hori-senpai!

15:17.380 --> 15:19.310
Happy Valentine's Day!

15:19.740 --> 15:21.310
This is for you!

15:21.310 --> 15:23.460
I worked really hard on it!

15:23.460 --> 15:24.930
Th-Thank you.

15:24.930 --> 15:27.320
<i>So this is what she said
she'd try her best on.</i>

15:27.690 --> 15:29.700
Wow, it's so cute!

15:29.700 --> 15:30.820
You really think so?

15:30.820 --> 15:32.070
I'm so glad!

15:32.070 --> 15:34.320
I love the color of this ribbon.

15:35.100 --> 15:37.080
I'm almost sad to open it.

15:37.650 --> 15:41.580
Miyamura told me what colors you like.

15:42.010 --> 15:45.590
He said you'd definitely like that one.

15:45.590 --> 15:48.280
I hated that I needed his help, but...

15:49.300 --> 15:52.150
<i>What I like...</i>

15:54.200 --> 15:55.150
<i>I see.</i>

15:56.100 --> 15:58.240
I love it. Thank you.

15:59.870 --> 16:03.700
<i>Maybe hoping to see someone you like 
with a happy look on their face</i>

16:04.550 --> 16:06.590
<i>is what today is really about.</i>

16:08.900 --> 16:12.000
Good, you're here! Package for you!

16:12.000 --> 16:13.110
What is it?

16:13.110 --> 16:14.940
Chocolate delivery.

16:14.940 --> 16:17.250
I'm giving them to everyone, 
so they're not very big,

16:17.250 --> 16:19.620
but they came out better than last year!

16:20.870 --> 16:22.870
<b>Smells funny</b>

16:22.870 --> 16:25.150
I'll eat mine at home!

16:25.150 --> 16:26.420
S-So will I.

16:26.420 --> 16:28.710
Don't wait too long to eat them. Bye!

16:29.700 --> 16:31.470
It's like a storm passed through.

16:31.470 --> 16:32.400
Yeah.

16:34.430 --> 16:35.820
Yoshikawa-san!

16:37.390 --> 16:38.650
Kono-san?

16:38.650 --> 16:40.890
Um, I didn't get a chance to give you this.

16:40.890 --> 16:42.050
Here.

16:43.760 --> 16:46.310
Okay, I'll give it to him.

16:46.310 --> 16:47.950
Thanks, but...

16:47.950 --> 16:50.900
Well, look inside later.

16:51.840 --> 16:52.740
Bye.

16:54.230 --> 16:56.130
<i>Is it okay to look inside?</i>

16:56.910 --> 16:58.910
Ishikawa-kun

16:56.910 --> 16:58.910
<i>There are two boxes.</i>

16:59.910 --> 17:01.910
Ishikawa-kun

16:59.910 --> 17:01.910
Yuki

17:05.540 --> 17:07.110
Kono-san...

17:08.070 --> 17:10.070
S-Sakura...

17:18.710 --> 17:20.060
Pardon me.

17:20.060 --> 17:21.430
Am I early?

17:21.430 --> 17:23.670
Nope, you're right on time.

17:23.670 --> 17:24.560
Have a seat.

17:25.010 --> 17:26.060
Where's your mom?

17:26.420 --> 17:28.280
She should be home soon.

17:33.210 --> 17:35.540
<i>What if he doesn't like them?</i>

17:37.780 --> 17:43.520
<i>Miyamura's so nice. He'll probably 
say he likes them even if he doesn't.</i>

17:44.340 --> 17:45.710
Thanks for waiting.

17:46.390 --> 17:47.460
Miyamura—

17:50.960 --> 17:52.960
Happy Valentine's.

17:53.000 --> 17:56.420
Oooh

17:54.220 --> 17:56.420
I tried making a Valentine cake.

17:57.050 --> 17:58.300
It smells so good!

17:58.300 --> 17:59.230
Can I eat it?

17:59.230 --> 18:00.970
Okay, I will! Thank you!

18:06.110 --> 18:08.980
<i>Delicious as always!</i>

18:08.980 --> 18:11.810
I'm so glad you like it.

18:11.810 --> 18:14.070
Why? Were you worried about it?

18:14.070 --> 18:16.740
Not worried exactly...

18:17.090 --> 18:20.540
Truth is, I couldn't decide how to wrap it.

18:20.540 --> 18:23.990
I would've brought it to your house otherwise.

18:24.540 --> 18:28.250
Sorry that it's so plain.

18:28.250 --> 18:30.250
<b><i>S
H
O
C
K</i></b>

18:30.250 --> 18:34.710
<i>I brought the chocolate I made 
without any kind of wrapping.</i>

18:30.250 --> 18:38.260
<b>Tremble</b>

18:30.250 --> 18:38.260
<b>Tremble</b>

18:30.250 --> 18:38.260
<b>Tremble</b>

18:30.250 --> 18:38.260
<b>Tremble</b>

18:34.710 --> 18:37.280
Not at all... I really like it...

18:37.280 --> 18:38.260
Really?

18:39.510 --> 18:41.010
<i>It's too late to worry now.</i>

18:41.010 --> 18:44.460
Actually, I made something, too.

18:41.010 --> 18:53.150
<b>Shake</b>

18:41.010 --> 18:53.150
<b>Shake</b>

18:41.010 --> 18:53.150
<b>Shake</b>

18:41.010 --> 18:53.150
<b>Shake</b>

18:44.460 --> 18:46.910
What? You made something for me?

18:46.910 --> 18:51.180
I'm sure you already know it won't be
nearly as good as yours.

18:51.180 --> 18:53.150
Why are you being so self-critical?

18:51.310 --> 18:52.020
<b><i>Droop</i></b>

18:53.990 --> 18:56.560
Wow, chocolate ganache.

18:56.560 --> 18:57.900
I love ganache.

18:57.900 --> 18:59.670
<i>I should've known...</i>

18:57.900 --> 19:04.160
<b>Depressed</b>

18:57.900 --> 19:04.160
<b>Happy</b>

18:59.670 --> 19:04.160
<i>On special occasions, you make 
something by hand and wrap it with care.</i>

19:04.160 --> 19:07.980
<i>I was only thinking about him eating it.</i>

19:07.980 --> 19:10.420
Oh, this plate is from your house.

19:10.750 --> 19:12.420
Kinda puts me at ease.

19:14.420 --> 19:16.420
<i>He's eaten a bunch of it.</i>

19:16.730 --> 19:18.060
Do you like it?

19:18.060 --> 19:19.150
I do.

19:19.150 --> 19:20.640
It's just sweet enough.

19:21.160 --> 19:22.930
Want to try one, Hori-san?

19:23.300 --> 19:25.180
Here. Say, "Aah."

19:27.100 --> 19:28.360
Pretty good, right?

19:28.360 --> 19:29.680
I guess...

19:30.520 --> 19:33.360
<i>It's better than my practice ones.</i>

19:33.890 --> 19:36.690
It's hard to relax until you see 
how your partner reacts.

19:40.380 --> 19:42.510
<i>So he felt the same way...</i>

19:43.250 --> 19:45.550
How is the cake?

19:45.920 --> 19:47.780
It's delicious, obviously.

19:47.780 --> 19:49.600
You made it, after all.

19:49.600 --> 19:51.210
Thank goodness.

19:53.610 --> 19:56.330
How am I supposed to eat 
with you staring at me?

19:56.330 --> 19:57.710
Oh, sorry.

19:58.090 --> 20:01.180
<i>Chocolate cake that 
simply melts in your mouth.</i>

20:01.640 --> 20:03.720
<i>Whipped cream that isn't too sweet.</i>

20:04.280 --> 20:05.710
<i>Just how I like it.</i>

20:05.710 --> 20:07.930
What should I make next year?

20:07.930 --> 20:08.970
It's too soon for that.

20:10.550 --> 20:11.980
You'll eat it, right?

20:13.790 --> 20:15.620
Of course I will.

20:15.620 --> 20:18.730
<i>It's something that only I'll get to taste.</i>

20:19.480 --> 20:21.900
What are you gonna make for me?

20:21.900 --> 20:24.110
I don't need to make anything anymore.

20:24.110 --> 20:27.390
You were so cute, 
looking worried all this time.

20:27.390 --> 20:28.830
Don't mind that!

20:28.830 --> 20:30.370
How could I not?

20:31.360 --> 20:33.640
<i>Miyamura put his heart into that dessert.</i>

20:33.640 --> 20:35.520
<i>It tasted like happiness.</i>

22:02.550 --> 22:06.010
Next time
page.12 Hori's House

22:11.390 --> 22:13.510
Oh, Sawada-san.

22:15.520 --> 22:18.030
The third-years are going home soon.

22:18.750 --> 22:19.760
Yeah.

22:20.910 --> 22:23.010
I just can't do it after all.

22:23.010 --> 22:25.530
I can't even talk to the boys in my class.

22:25.860 --> 22:27.890
I'm just making up excuses.

22:29.290 --> 22:33.870
All after you were such a big help...
I'm sorry.

22:34.520 --> 22:35.790
I can give it to—

22:37.100 --> 22:39.290
<i>That's not the issue here.</i>

22:41.020 --> 22:44.050
<i>She wanted to give it to him herself.</i>

22:44.050 --> 22:46.460
Now this will go to waste.

22:46.460 --> 22:49.240
But I was so excited, 
and that was really fun.

22:50.220 --> 22:51.550
Thank you.

22:53.380 --> 22:55.060
Okay, then give me the chocolate!

22:55.750 --> 22:58.400
You said I could have it 
if you didn't give it to him.

22:58.400 --> 23:00.040
That way, it won't go to waste.

23:00.040 --> 23:01.560
I'll eat all of it.

23:02.790 --> 23:03.860
Really?

23:05.120 --> 23:07.070
You'll really eat it?

23:08.950 --> 23:09.820
Okay, then...

23:11.450 --> 23:12.230
Here.

23:12.230 --> 23:13.400
Thanks.

23:14.070 --> 23:19.270
And this... is from me.

23:20.300 --> 23:22.050
I bought it yesterday.

23:22.050 --> 23:24.090
I guess it's obligatory chocolate or whatever.

23:25.460 --> 23:27.170
Thank you, Sawada-san.

23:28.120 --> 23:30.340
But this isn't obligatory chocolate.

23:30.340 --> 23:34.260
Hoping you have a Happy Valentine's Day.
-Sawada

23:30.950 --> 23:32.970
It's friendship chocolate.
